board:0012 b1df object-model fix (CORRECTS patch 258) + the effect spawn/despawn/render cascade it unblocks.
ROOT: b21d (0x1b21d) is the pool allocator -- AX=type/class key IN, DI=new object near-offset OUT (it does
NOT read incoming DI).  FUN_1000_b1a2 (patch 200) uses b21d's returned DI correctly; FUN_1000_b1df (patch
258) did NOT -- it ran b21d (a294++, allocating a slot) but registered the CALLER's param_2 and dropped
b21d's DI, ORPHANING a pool slot every call and never producing the fresh object callers need.  That single
bug is the root of the a294 leak AND of "units never fire".  This patch (all asm-verified vs
fist_dat_image.bin) fixes b1df to allocate+register+return b21d's DI, threads the fresh object through the
effect spawners ba33/ba49 (asm: mov si,di; ba5d(template,si); ba49 writes velocity to SI), and migrates the
now-reachable effect DESPAWN (bab4 type-4 update -> b354->b2ef, + its DI-threaded frame handlers bae1/bb02,
all base-lost) and the RENDER method c694 (word[si+0x1c] was a host-ptr; c945/c962 already migrated).
RESULT: the in-mission effect lifecycle runs with NO crash, NO stub, NO guard; the AZER1 self-play sim runs
to completion (exit 0); native==wasm==ref central-chrome AE=0; 25/0 native matrix.  This does NOT by itself
resolve combat (the per-tick AI FIRE dispatch 7e29/899c/91b8/99a2 + spawn methods 7745/778a/77cf/7814 remain
-- the board carries their exact asm-verified C); it is the object-model foundation those build on.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -32315,8 +32315,9 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_c694(undefined2 param_1,undefined2 param_2,int param_3,undefined2 param_4)
 
 {
-  DAT_2000_a3b4 = 0x3e800;
-  FUN_0000_c945(param_1,param_2,*(undefined2 *)(param_3 + 0x1c),param_3,param_4);
+  DAT_2000_a3b4 = 0x3e800;    /* PATCH 424: si=object near-offset; word[si+0x1c] DGROUP-based (asm mov bp,[si+0x1c]) */
+  { unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+    FUN_0000_c945(param_1,param_2,*(unsigned short *)(dg + (unsigned short)(param_3 + 0x1c)),param_3,param_4); }
   return;
 }
 
